  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Today is the start of our annual end-of-year fundraising drive. More than half of our entire annual operating budget is raised around these final few weeks of the year, and our goal is to raise $350,000. We count on your giving-season generosity to make a tax-deductible donation to keep NutritionFacts.org going and growing.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This year is the tenth anniversary of NutritionFacts.org. Before the organization was founded, I traveled around the country giving hundreds of presentations about lifestyle medicine each year. Then, the Jesse &amp; Julie Rasch Foundation generously provided the seed money to launch the organization and website in order to reach even more people with this life-changing, life-saving information. Now, we rely on the support of individual donors like you. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A lot has changed in the last ten years. Today, more than a dozen staff members keep the engines running. Just this past year, we hired four new positions to help expand our outreach and web development programs. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is all thanks to the support of our donors. As you know, there are no ads or corporate sponsors on NutritionFacts.org. Our supporters are truly the lifeblood of this organization. You enable us to do this work. Every year, thousands of people step forward and make donations large and small to express appreciation for our work. Hundreds have even signed up to be monthly donors, which helps ensure a predictable and steady stream of support. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Please “root” for the facts by helping us fill the carrot during our year-end funding drive! It’s a numbers game; even a single dollar can help.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For the second year in a row, a generous donor is providing a $100,000 match. Make your contributions early to have them doubled! </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">On the </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Donate Page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, you can make a tax-deductible donation </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/donate/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">using a credit card or PayPal</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. You can also transfer </span><a href=\"https://www.stockdonator.com/stock-information/?oid=c9fe74\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">stock</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> or mail a check to NutritionFacts.org, 6800 Wisconsin Avenue #1185 Chevy Chase, MD 20815. Federal employees can even donate through the CFC workplace giving program with designation number 26461.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Your Donations Help Change Lives</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/Jack.png/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-70882 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/Jack-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/Jack-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/Jack-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/Jack-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/Jack-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/Jack-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/Jack-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/Jack.png 1080w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>“I was raised on the standard American diet, and by the time I was approaching 40, I hit my highest weight at 240. I can still remember that day. It’s when I’d had enough. I started to research nutrition, and your site was the first I came across. It changed my life. I have two young children, and I want to be around for them as long as I can without being a burden either. I lost my Mom at 43 and my Dad at 65, and I don’t want my kids to experience what I did. I also want to set a good example for them.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Now, at nearly 49 years old, I feel and look better than I have at any point in my life. People think I’m around 35. I can hike and bike for miles on end, run football routes with my 9-year-old son, and play basketball with him and his friends. When I was at my heaviest, my doctor wanted to put me on a statin; dietary changes were never mentioned. But, I wanted to fix it myself. My doctor now calls my lipid profile and blood work ‘remarkable.’ Learning about nutrition, calorie density, and plant-based diets is the single greatest self improvement I’ve ever done. And I thank you and all of your colleagues for the information to help me succeed. Hopefully I can influence the people around me, too!” –Jack</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Key Takeaways: Cocoa</b></h4>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-70880 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/cocoa-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/cocoa-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/cocoa-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/cocoa-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/cocoa-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/cocoa-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/cocoa-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/cocoa.jpg 1080w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Although we should avoid processed chocolate due to the sugar content, cocoa has a number of health benefits. What are they? Find out on the </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/cocoa/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">topic page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Recipe: Champurrado</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/champurrado-3-e1639160189314.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-70876 size-large alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/champurrado-3-e1639160189314-1024x1022.jpg\" alt=\"mexican cocoa\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/champurrado-3-e1639160189314-1024x1022.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/champurrado-3-e1639160189314-960x958.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/champurrado-3-e1639160189314-768x766.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/champurrado-3-e1639160189314-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/champurrado-3-e1639160189314-1200x1197.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/champurrado-3-e1639160189314-720x718.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/champurrado-3-e1639160189314-540x539.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Now that you know about the benefits of cocoa, try our recipe for this traditional Mexican drink. Get the free recipe </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/champurrado/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and see how it’s made on our </span><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/CUF2VauJE8x/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Instagram</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. </span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Books Available Around the World</b></h4>\n<p>\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/translated-books.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-70900 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/12/translated-books.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"280\"/></a>Still looking for holiday gifts? My books are available in several countries. In fact, the paperback version of </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet-cookbook/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The How Not to Diet Cookbook</span></i></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> was just published in the United Kingdom! Check out our </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4406241003035-How-to-order-the-books-in-another-country\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">help center article</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to see where and how to purchase my books globally.</span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">And, as always, all proceeds from my books are donated to charity. </span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-large wp-image-60211\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png\" alt=\"Top 3 Videos of the Month\" width=\"460\" height=\"149\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-960x310.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-768x248.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-720x233.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-540x174.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png 1108w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 460px) 100vw, 460px\"/></a></h4>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-25-Extra-Virgin-Olive-Oil-for-Arthritis.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-68503 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-25-Extra-Virgin-Olive-Oil-for-Arthritis-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Olives and olive oil on white background\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-25-Extra-Virgin-Olive-Oil-for-Arthritis-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-25-Extra-Virgin-Olive-Oil-for-Arthritis-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-25-Extra-Virgin-Olive-Oil-for-Arthritis-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-25-Extra-Virgin-Olive-Oil-for-Arthritis-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-25-Extra-Virgin-Olive-Oil-for-Arthritis-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-25-Extra-Virgin-Olive-Oil-for-Arthritis-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-25-Extra-Virgin-Olive-Oil-for-Arthritis-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-25-Extra-Virgin-Olive-Oil-for-Arthritis.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/extra-virgin-olive-oil-for-arthritis/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Extra Virgin Olive Oil for Arthritis</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> – What happened when topical olive oil was pitted against an ibuprofen-type drug for osteoarthritis and rheumatoid arthritis?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-26-Are-Onions-Beneficial-for-Testosterone-Osteoporosis-Allergies-and-Cancer.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-68510 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-26-Are-Onions-Beneficial-for-Testosterone-Osteoporosis-Allergies-and-Cancer-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"natural organic onions of different varieties\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-26-Are-Onions-Beneficial-for-Testosterone-Osteoporosis-Allergies-and-Cancer-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-26-Are-Onions-Beneficial-for-Testosterone-Osteoporosis-Allergies-and-Cancer-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-26-Are-Onions-Beneficial-for-Testosterone-Osteoporosis-Allergies-and-Cancer-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-26-Are-Onions-Beneficial-for-Testosterone-Osteoporosis-Allergies-and-Cancer-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-26-Are-Onions-Beneficial-for-Testosterone-Osteoporosis-Allergies-and-Cancer-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-26-Are-Onions-Beneficial-for-Testosterone-Osteoporosis-Allergies-and-Cancer-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-26-Are-Onions-Beneficial-for-Testosterone-Osteoporosis-Allergies-and-Cancer-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-26-Are-Onions-Beneficial-for-Testosterone-Osteoporosis-Allergies-and-Cancer.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/are-onions-beneficial-for-testosterone-osteoporosis-allergies-and-cancer/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Are Onions Beneficial for Testosterone, Osteoporosis, Allergies, and Cancer?</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> – What did randomized controlled human trials find about the ways we may—or may not—benefit from eating onions?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-20-Are-Baruka-Nuts-the-Healthiest-Nut.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-68480 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-20-Are-Baruka-Nuts-the-Healthiest-Nut-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Assorted nuts on black background\" width=\"215\" height=\"121\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-20-Are-Baruka-Nuts-the-Healthiest-Nut-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-20-Are-Baruka-Nuts-the-Healthiest-Nut-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-20-Are-Baruka-Nuts-the-Healthiest-Nut-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-20-Are-Baruka-Nuts-the-Healthiest-Nut-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-20-Are-Baruka-Nuts-the-Healthiest-Nut-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-20-Are-Baruka-Nuts-the-Healthiest-Nut-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-20-Are-Baruka-Nuts-the-Healthiest-Nut-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/08/55-20-Are-Baruka-Nuts-the-Healthiest-Nut.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 215px) 100vw, 215px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/are-baruka-nuts-the-healthiest-nut/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Are Baruka Nuts the Healthiest Nut?</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">  – How do barukas, also known as baru almonds, compare with other nuts?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Live Q&amp;As </b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-68737 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"image of dr greger\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Due to my writing schedule for my next book, </span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Not to Age</span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, I will be taking a break from Q&amp;As until summer 2022. In the meantime, you can find links to past live Q&amp;As </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> on NutritionFacts.org. And, remember, I have an </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/audio/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">audio podcast</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to keep you company, too.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></a></li>\n</ul>"
